(/ Sean compiler notes

- 10M LOC/s should be possible in theory.
- lexer: state machine transitions, split char stream into spans, pooling spans per first-char classify or maybe final state machine state.
- code generation: do dumb register allocation pass first, and then observe its spilling behaviour. Use a second register allocator that can then optimise the register allocation to reduce spills.
- Per Vognsen talks about single-pass compilers? bitwise project.
