	it seems like it's too hard to beat a simple sequential load chain. So we would have 5-6 cycles per byte, being the latency of loading from L1. Better than 20-25 cycles any day, but still disappointing. 3-4 would have been pretty cool, but SWAR LUTs need lots of chained instructions. If we had a native instruction for u4x16[i], then that would change things, as we could get something like 3 cycles per byte. Anyway, with this, we can surely ditch one of the tokeniser threads, reducing contention, etc.. And at that point, the other threads would bottleneck anyway. It would still benefit us more to have  /)